# Vendor RTC SDK binaries / headers — proprietary, never commit. Both
# the OS-level vendor location (`~/codes/vendor/DingRTC_*_SDK_*/` — lives
# outside any repo, no .gitignore needed for it) and any in-tree
# placement under `deploy/edge/*/vendor/` are covered here.
#
# Post-`engine-rtc-dingrtc-migration` § 7 the canonical SDK is DingRTC
# 3.9.0; the legacy AliRTC Windows lines remain in place until § 7.9
# physically deletes the legacy `deploy/edge/windows/vendor/aliyun-artc-windows/`
# tree from this repo's Windows checkouts. The DingRTC globs are
# forward-compat — they kick in the moment someone unpacks a vendor zip
# into the in-tree path.

# DingRTC (post-§ 7)
vendor/DingRTC_*_SDK_*/
deploy/edge/windows/vendor/dingrtc-windows/
deploy/edge/macos/vendor/DingRTC_*_SDK_*/

# Legacy ApsaraVideo Live ARTC SDK for Windows (pre-§ 7) — delete the
# three lines below in the same commit that runs § 7.9 cleanup on the
# Windows dev rig.
deploy/edge/windows/vendor/aliyun-artc-windows/include/
deploy/edge/windows/vendor/aliyun-artc-windows/x64/
deploy/edge/windows/vendor/aliyun-artc-windows/x86/

# Secrets / tokens — never commit
*.jwt
.edge-token-*
scripts/_pybind_join_probe.py
